      "content": "i get the apophenia thing but it wasnt just a feeling, it was mathematical. the way the order book depth shifted was literally following a fractal pattern that matched my focus cycle. if you look at the way HFT systems use machine learning to predict 'human' volatility, isn't it possible they've actually tuned themselves to pick up on certain bio-rhythms or electromagnetic spikes from highly concentrated intent? like, if the algos are trained on human behavior, could they be accidentally sync'ing with it on a sub-second level? it feels like there's a feedback loop there that the standard models don't account for.",
